WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.840
Augustine faced a grim
puzzle about the end of time.

2
00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:08.840
What happens to a body that is burnt,
eaten or scattered to the winds?

3
00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:12.890
The old Latin creed speaks of
the resurrection of the flesh.

4
00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:17.640
Yet Paul writes that the body is
sown natural and raised spiritual.

5
00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:21.580
If Christians will rise from the dead,
will they get back the same body,

6
00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:23.160
or a new kind?

7
00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:25.780
In this mission, you'll
test Augustine's answer,

8
00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:27.600
from his City of God.

9
00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:31.770
Then you'll read Paul's four
contrasts in 1 Corinthians 15,

10
00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:33.970
and his picture of a seed.

11
00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:38.430
Your mission: find out what Christians
believe about the resurrected body.
